+
+Frontend half of Phase 2. Two chips and a single SSE subscription per
+FileRow:
+
+- <FileStatusChip pathStatus={…}/>: composes German status text (mount /
+  inline / rag), aggregate color (success / warn / error / pending),
+  tooltip with failure reason. Defensive against undefined / null /
+  empty pathStatus (Pre-Phase-3 file rows / FILE_ROUTING_V2 OFF — S5
+  stale-risk-hoch). Mount-failed (T-34 MIME-Filter) takes priority and
+  surfaces the actionable reason inline.
+
+- <SessionFileChip sessionFile={…}/>: code-generated files from
+  Conversation.session_files (Phase 3 Track 2). Real schema is
+  { session_id, file_id, filename, generated_at } — no path/kind, so
+  one render path, "📦 <filename> · vom Code generiert" + tooltip.
+
+- useFileStatusStream({ enabled, conversationId, initialSessionFiles }):
+  single sse.js connection per FileRow with explicit Bearer token
+  (LibreChat's requireJwtAuth uses header-only auth — native EventSource
+  won't work). Fans out per-file pathStatus updates and conversation-
+  level session_file events. Initial sessionFiles seeded from
+  conversation.session_files; live updates merged with dedup on
+  (session_id, file_id).
+
+- FileContainer renders the chip below the filetype text when path-
+  Status is present (live or cached at upload-time). FileRow mounts
+  the hook once and threads pathStatus down per file_id; renders
+  SessionFileChip row below the file row.
+
+Tests: 50 unit tests (FileStatusChip, SessionFileChip, hook with mock
+sse.js). Existing FileRow tests updated with new mocks.
+
